{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "35734812",
      "title": "Submitting Data with action()s",
      "sourceHash": "1921291e42c1237bd539d3464290560ad601af9bc0dbe7ddcdc0816354f1f443",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.16,
          "end": 4.14,
          "en": "So it's great that we can now load data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.14,
          "end": 5.82,
          "en": "with that loader feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.82,
          "end": 7.5,
          "en": "but what about submitting data?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.5,
          "end": 9.09,
          "en": "What about creating a new post?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.09,
          "end": 10.92,
          "en": "At the moment, this doesn't work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 10.92,
          "end": 12.45,
          "en": "And of course, it should work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 12.45,
          "end": 15.543,
          "en": "And for that, we can also leverage React Router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 16.44,
          "end": 17.91,
          "en": "It's the NewPost component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 17.91,
          "end": 20.73,
          "en": "where we have this form in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 20.73,
          "end": 21.9,
          "en": "And we've got a bunch of code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 21.9,
          "end": 24.09,
          "en": "for getting the user input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 24.09,
          "end": 27.51,
          "en": "and for then preventing the default behavior of the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 27.51,
          "end": 29.823,
          "en": "and doing something with the data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 31.02,
          "end": 32.28,
          "en": "Now, what we could do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 32.28,
          "end": 34.92,
          "en": "is we could grab that code for sending that data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 34.92,
          "end": 36.33,
          "en": "to the backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 36.33,
          "end": 38.76,
          "en": "and cut it from addPostHandler here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 38.76,
          "end": 40.98,
          "en": "and actually get rid of addPostHandler",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 40.98,
          "end": 44.64,
          "en": "in PostsList, making this component even leaner.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 44.64,
          "end": 46.5,
          "en": "And instead add it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 46.5,
          "end": 48.21,
          "en": "in this NewPost component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 48.21,
          "end": 51.603,
          "en": "instead of calling onAddPost and onCancel.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 53.04,
          "end": 56.01,
          "en": "Instead of doing that, we could send that postData",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 56.01,
          "end": 59.673,
          "en": "to the backend right from inside the NewPost component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 60.78,
          "end": 62.94,
          "en": "And indeed, this would work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 62.94,
          "end": 65.43,
          "en": "but it's still a bunch of code we would have to write here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 65.43,
          "end": 66.99,
          "en": "especially since we probably",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 66.99,
          "end": 69.48,
          "en": "also wanna close the modal thereafter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 69.48,
          "end": 72.09,
          "en": "which means that we then also have to add extra code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 72.09,
          "end": 75.063,
          "en": "for navigating to a different route programmatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 76.35,
          "end": 78.66,
          "en": "A better and more elegant approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 78.66,
          "end": 81.21000000000001,
          "en": "is to also use a special feature offered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 81.21000000000001,
          "end": 82.95,
          "en": "by React Router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 82.95,
          "end": 86.03999999999999,
          "en": "because just as you can add loaders to your routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 86.03999999999999,
          "end": 88.65,
          "en": "to load data before it gets activated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 88.65,
          "end": 91.08,
          "en": "and before the component gets rendered,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 91.08,
          "end": 93.99000000000001,
          "en": "you can add actions to routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 93.99000000000001,
          "end": 96.39,
          "en": "So to this route here, the create-post route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 96.39,
          "end": 99.99000000000001,
          "en": "we can add an action by setting the action property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 99.99000000000001,
          "end": 102.9,
          "en": "And just like loader, action wants a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 102.9,
          "end": 103.833,
          "en": "as a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 105,
          "end": 107.37,
          "en": "This function, however, will now be triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 107.37,
          "end": 110.49000000000001,
          "en": "when a form is submitted in that route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 110.49000000000001,
          "end": 113.28,
          "en": "which means that here in the NewPost component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 113.28,
          "end": 116.49000000000001,
          "en": "we could export such a action function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 116.49000000000001,
          "end": 119.07,
          "en": "to again have that code close to the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 119.07,
          "end": 120.78,
          "en": "to which it belongs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 120.78,
          "end": 122.7,
          "en": "And then in here, we could add our code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 122.7,
          "end": 125.55,
          "en": "for sending that request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 125.55,
          "end": 126.383,
          "en": "Like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 127.29,
          "end": 128.37,
          "en": "Now, we still need to get the postData",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 128.37,
          "end": 131.49,
          "en": "but that's how we could get started.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 131.49,
          "end": 133.23,
          "en": "But how do we now get the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 133.23,
          "end": 135.813,
          "en": "that's entered into the form by the user?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 136.77,
          "end": 140.04,
          "en": "Well, previously, we had to manage our own state for that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 140.04,
          "end": 142.32,
          "en": "Now when we embrace React Router,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 142.32,
          "end": 144.84,
          "en": "this all gets much leaner again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 144.84,
          "end": 146.67000000000002,
          "en": "We can delete that state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 146.67000000000002,
          "end": 150.03,
          "en": "and delete these functions that updated the state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 150.03,
          "end": 152.61,
          "en": "We can also delete this submitHandler",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 152.61,
          "end": 155.403,
          "en": "and therefore, also delete the useState import.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 156.45,
          "end": 159.32999999999998,
          "en": "And get rid of the onSubmit event listener",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 159.32999999999998,
          "end": 160.62,
          "en": "on the form element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 160.62,
          "end": 164.703,
          "en": "and get rid of the onChange listeners on the inputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 165.84,
          "end": 168.66,
          "en": "So we already got rid of a lot of code here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 168.66,
          "end": 170.61,
          "en": "And instead, all we have to do here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 170.61,
          "end": 174.18,
          "en": "is add a name attribute to our inputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 174.18,
          "end": 176.88,
          "en": "So in this case, to the text area here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 176.88,
          "end": 178.47,
          "en": "And then assign a name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 178.47,
          "end": 180.9,
          "en": "which we later wanna use for extracting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 180.9,
          "end": 182.76,
          "en": "and submitting our data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 182.76,
          "end": 186.06,
          "en": "So for example, here my posts have a body,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 186.06,
          "end": 188.19,
          "en": "and an author field here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 188.19,
          "end": 192.18,
          "en": "And if I wanna stick to that to body and author,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 192.18,
          "end": 196.41,
          "en": "I could give my text area here the name body,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 196.41,
          "end": 199.503,
          "en": "and this here, the name author.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 200.82,
          "end": 202.47,
          "en": "So that I already used the keys",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 202.47,
          "end": 205.11,
          "en": "which I wanna use for storing my data here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 205.11,
          "end": 206.313,
          "en": "on these inputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 207.15,
          "end": 210.54,
          "en": "But what's the idea behind this name attribute?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 210.54,
          "end": 212.85,
          "en": "Well, it's a default HTML attribute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 212.85,
          "end": 214.95,
          "en": "that can be added to form inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 214.95,
          "end": 217.2,
          "en": "and by default, if a form is submitted,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 217.2,
          "end": 219.48,
          "en": "the browser will, as mentioned earlier,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 219.48,
          "end": 220.92000000000002,
          "en": "generate a request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 220.92000000000002,
          "end": 222.99,
          "en": "and it will try to send it to the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 222.99,
          "end": 225.15,
          "en": "that served that website,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 225.15,
          "end": 226.2,
          "en": "which would be wrong",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 226.2,
          "end": 228.81,
          "en": "because that server that's serving that website",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 228.81,
          "end": 231.87,
          "en": "doesn't have any code to handle this request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 231.87,
          "end": 233.85,
          "en": "with the form data on the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 233.85,
          "end": 237.153,
          "en": "because we have no backend code as part of this React app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 237.99,
          "end": 241.05,
          "en": "But that's now where React Router comes in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 241.05,
          "end": 244.5,
          "en": "We can import a special component from React Router,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 244.5,
          "end": 247.473,
          "en": "and that would be the Form component with a capital F.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 249.18,
          "end": 250.8,
          "en": "And if we use that instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 250.8,
          "end": 254.13,
          "en": "of the regular built-in Form element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 254.13,
          "end": 256.95,
          "en": "React Router will handle the form submission",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 256.95,
          "end": 259.47,
          "en": "and it will prevent that browser default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 259.47,
          "end": 261.21,
          "en": "of sending a request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 261.21,
          "end": 264.06,
          "en": "but it will still gather all the input data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 264.06,
          "end": 267.9,
          "en": "still generate an object with that data for us,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 267.9,
          "end": 269.85,
          "en": "and that's the important part,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 269.85,
          "end": 273.48,
          "en": "call the action that is assigned to the route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 273.48,
          "end": 274.83,
          "en": "which contains the form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 274.83,
          "end": 276.873,
          "en": "the form with the capital F.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 278.34000000000003,
          "end": 281.22,
          "en": "So therefore now with this Form component being used,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 281.22,
          "end": 283.128,
          "en": "React Router will in the end make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 283.128,
          "end": 286.32,
          "en": "that this action here gets executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 286.32,
          "end": 290.61,
          "en": "and therefore, we can now also import this action function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 290.61,
          "end": 293.64,
          "en": "which I'm exporting here in NewPost.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 293.64,
          "end": 297.48,
          "en": "Import this from the NewPost component file here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 297.48,
          "end": 298.8,
          "en": "The action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 298.8,
          "end": 300.69,
          "en": "And maybe also give it an alias",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 300.69,
          "end": 302.19,
          "en": "in case we had multiple actions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 302.19,
          "end": 305.1,
          "en": "from different routes to avoid clashes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 305.1,
          "end": 307.563,
          "en": "That could be the newPostAction therefore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 308.55,
          "end": 310.26,
          "en": "And assign that as a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 310.26,
          "end": 313.053,
          "en": "for the action property down there, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 314.49,
          "end": 315.99,
          "en": "So that in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 315.99,
          "end": 318.24,
          "en": "it's now this action function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 318.24,
          "end": 320.46,
          "en": "that will be executed by React Router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 320.46,
          "end": 322.83299999999997,
          "en": "if this form here is submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 324.27,
          "end": 326.01,
          "en": "Now one last thing I'll do here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 326.01,
          "end": 328.29,
          "en": "is I'll add the method prop here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 328.29,
          "end": 331.5,
          "en": "to this Form component and set it to post.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 331.5,
          "end": 332.97,
          "en": "Now, it's important to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 332.97,
          "end": 336.54,
          "en": "that no actual post request will be sent anywhere",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 336.54,
          "end": 338.90999999999997,
          "en": "because this is still all client-side code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 338.90999999999997,
          "end": 341.19,
          "en": "but what React Router will do behind the scenes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 341.19,
          "end": 343.86,
          "en": "is it will generate a request object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 343.86,
          "end": 346.83,
          "en": "with that form data included in it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 346.83,
          "end": 349.83,
          "en": "And it will give this request object a method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 349.83,
          "end": 352.2,
          "en": "which we could then use here on the action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 352.2,
          "end": 355.14,
          "en": "to find out which form was submitted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 355.14,
          "end": 356.55,
          "en": "when this cation was triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 356.55,
          "end": 358.40999999999997,
          "en": "in case we had multiple forms",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 358.40999999999997,
          "end": 361.263,
          "en": "that belong to the same route with the same action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 362.22,
          "end": 364.92,
          "en": "And even without that, it's kind of a good idea",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 364.92,
          "end": 368.67,
          "en": "to use the semantically correct HTTP verb",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 368.67,
          "end": 370.77,
          "en": "and since we're creating a new post here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 370.77,
          "end": 372.75,
          "en": "the post method makes sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 372.75,
          "end": 375.21,
          "en": "because that's typically the HTTP method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 375.21,
          "end": 378.24,
          "en": "that is used for creating resources.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 378.24,
          "end": 380.88,
          "en": "So with that, no request is sent to the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 380.88,
          "end": 383.13,
          "en": "Instead, this action will be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 147,
          "start": 383.13,
          "end": 387.48,
          "en": "and here, you actually get some data argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 148,
          "start": 387.48,
          "end": 391.02,
          "en": "This is passed in automatically by React Router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 149,
          "start": 391.02,
          "end": 392.73,
          "en": "And that's not the data of the form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 150,
          "start": 392.73,
          "end": 394.56,
          "en": "instead that is an object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 151,
          "start": 394.56,
          "end": 397.17,
          "en": "which for example, has a request property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 152,
          "start": 397.17,
          "end": 400.02,
          "en": "with that request object that's generated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 153,
          "start": 400.02,
          "end": 402.51,
          "en": "and built by React Router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 154,
          "start": 402.51,
          "end": 405.09000000000003,
          "en": "So React Router calls this action function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 155,
          "start": 405.09000000000003,
          "end": 407.13,
          "en": "and passes this object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 156,
          "start": 407.13,
          "end": 408.84000000000003,
          "en": "that includes the request object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 157,
          "start": 408.84000000000003,
          "end": 411.933,
          "en": "that was generated to this action function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 158,
          "start": 412.92,
          "end": 415.95,
          "en": "Therefore here, we can actually use object destructuring",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 159,
          "start": 415.95,
          "end": 419.04,
          "en": "to get hold of that request object like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 160,
          "start": 419.04,
          "end": 422.403,
          "en": "And now this request object has a formData method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 161,
          "start": 423.42,
          "end": 425.97,
          "en": "And when you execute that formData method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 162,
          "start": 425.97,
          "end": 429.24,
          "en": "you get access to the data encoded in that form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 163,
          "start": 429.24,
          "end": 432.45,
          "en": "so the data that was extracted by React Router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 164,
          "start": 432.45,
          "end": 436.803,
          "en": "when it analyzed that form and called that action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 165,
          "start": 438.09,
          "end": 440.25,
          "en": "Now, formData actually yields a promise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 166,
          "start": 440.25,
          "end": 442.23,
          "en": "so we should turn this into a async function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 167,
          "start": 442.23,
          "end": 444.42,
          "en": "so that we can use await.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 168,
          "start": 444.42,
          "end": 447.36,
          "en": "And then here we got our formData object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 169,
          "start": 447.36,
          "end": 450.27,
          "en": "And that is a rather complex object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 170,
          "start": 450.27,
          "end": 452.76,
          "en": "It's not a plain key-value store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 171,
          "start": 452.76,
          "end": 454.62,
          "en": "Instead, it's a object that, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 172,
          "start": 454.62,
          "end": 456.15,
          "en": "has a get method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 173,
          "start": 456.15,
          "end": 458.58,
          "en": "which you could call to get the value provided",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 174,
          "start": 458.58,
          "end": 460.773,
          "en": "for the body field, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 175,
          "start": 461.82,
          "end": 464.04,
          "en": "That's how you could then extract the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 176,
          "start": 464.04,
          "end": 466.8,
          "en": "that was provided by the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 177,
          "start": 466.8,
          "end": 468.65999999999997,
          "en": "Now, an easier approach here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 178,
          "start": 468.65999999999997,
          "end": 471.75,
          "en": "is to instead create a postData constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 179,
          "start": 471.75,
          "end": 474.24,
          "en": "and use the built-in Object class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 180,
          "start": 474.24,
          "end": 478.803,
          "en": "and call fromEntries and pass this formData object to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 181,
          "start": 479.94,
          "end": 481.98,
          "en": "Under the hood, this will simply then create",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 182,
          "start": 481.98,
          "end": 484.62,
          "en": "a basic key-value object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 183,
          "start": 484.62,
          "end": 485.97,
          "en": "where you have a body key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 184,
          "start": 485.97,
          "end": 489.93,
          "en": "with some value, and an author key with some value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 185,
          "start": 489.93,
          "end": 492.87,
          "en": "in our case here since we have body and author",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 186,
          "start": 492.87,
          "end": 496.023,
          "en": "as named values in this form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 187,
          "start": 497.43,
          "end": 499.74,
          "en": "So that's how we can extract the formData",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 188,
          "start": 499.74,
          "end": 501.45,
          "en": "with help of React Router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 189,
          "start": 501.45,
          "end": 504.753,
          "en": "Again, all still happening on the client side here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 190,
          "start": 505.71,
          "end": 507.93,
          "en": "And therefore now we got the postData we need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 191,
          "start": 507.93,
          "end": 509.343,
          "en": "for sending that request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 192,
          "start": 510.39,
          "end": 512.61,
          "en": "Here we can also await this to wait",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 193,
          "start": 512.61,
          "end": 514.5,
          "en": "for the request to be sent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 194,
          "start": 514.5,
          "end": 516.27,
          "en": "We could also get the response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 195,
          "start": 516.27,
          "end": 518.07,
          "en": "and analyze the response,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 196,
          "start": 518.07,
          "end": 521.37,
          "en": "for example, to find out if something went wrong",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 197,
          "start": 521.37,
          "end": 523.44,
          "en": "but I'll not do that here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 198,
          "start": 523.44,
          "end": 526.8,
          "en": "And instead now, after sending this request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 199,
          "start": 526.8,
          "end": 530.13,
          "en": "we can also call another function provided",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 200,
          "start": 530.13,
          "end": 531.57,
          "en": "by react-router-dom",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 201,
          "start": 531.57,
          "end": 533.57,
          "en": "and that would be the redirect function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 202,
          "start": 534.93,
          "end": 537.27,
          "en": "This is imported from react-router-dom",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 203,
          "start": 537.27,
          "end": 541.2,
          "en": "and you can call it in your action and loader functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 204,
          "start": 541.2,
          "end": 544.713,
          "en": "to return the result of calling this function here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 205,
          "start": 545.7,
          "end": 549.42,
          "en": "Now, what redirect does is it generates a response object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 206,
          "start": 549.42,
          "end": 551.91,
          "en": "which in the end is then returned by this action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 207,
          "start": 551.91,
          "end": 554.46,
          "en": "And if you return such a response object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 208,
          "start": 554.46,
          "end": 557.1,
          "en": "React Router will look into that object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 209,
          "start": 557.1,
          "end": 558.81,
          "en": "and if it's a redirect response,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 210,
          "start": 558.81,
          "end": 561.36,
          "en": "which is the kind of response that is generated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 211,
          "start": 561.36,
          "end": 564.63,
          "en": "by calling redirect, React Router will simply move",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 212,
          "start": 564.63,
          "end": 565.98,
          "en": "to that different route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 213,
          "start": 565.98,
          "end": 568.5,
          "en": "to which you're trying to redirect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 214,
          "start": 568.5,
          "end": 571.17,
          "en": "So here we could path a path of slash here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 215,
          "start": 571.17,
          "end": 574.23,
          "en": "to make sure that after this action was called,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 216,
          "start": 574.23,
          "end": 578.85,
          "en": "we actually make React Router load a different route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 217,
          "start": 578.85,
          "end": 581.07,
          "en": "the route with the path slash,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 218,
          "start": 581.07,
          "end": 583.95,
          "en": "which in this case is, of course, this route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 219,
          "start": 583.95,
          "end": 586.11,
          "en": "So that we leave the create-post route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 220,
          "start": 586.11,
          "end": 588.27,
          "en": "and we move to this route instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 221,
          "start": 588.27,
          "end": 592.2,
          "en": "That's how we can initialize this navigation action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 222,
          "start": 592.2,
          "end": 594.9,
          "en": "Again, all performed by React Router here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 223,
          "start": 594.9,
          "end": 597.33,
          "en": "There is no backend code involved here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 224,
          "start": 597.33,
          "end": 599.52,
          "en": "We're just sending a request to the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 225,
          "start": 599.52,
          "end": 602.43,
          "en": "but this code here all runs on the client side",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 226,
          "start": 602.43,
          "end": 604.23,
          "en": "in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 227,
          "start": 604.23,
          "end": 607.14,
          "en": "But with that all added, if we save everything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 228,
          "start": 607.14,
          "end": 610.8,
          "en": "and we go back and go to the New Post area",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 229,
          "start": 610.8,
          "end": 615.123,
          "en": "and try to add a new post, like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 230,
          "start": 615.96,
          "end": 618.09,
          "en": "you see I am redirected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 231,
          "start": 618.09,
          "end": 619.92,
          "en": "This new post shows up here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 232,
          "start": 619.92,
          "end": 622.26,
          "en": "If I reload, it still shows up here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 233,
          "start": 622.26,
          "end": 624.48,
          "en": "so it was indeed sent to the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 234,
          "start": 624.48,
          "end": 626.892,
          "en": "We can also see it in posts.json there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 235,
          "start": 626.892,
          "end": 630.45,
          "en": "And therefore, this proves that this action works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 236,
          "start": 630.45,
          "end": 631.44,
          "en": "the way it should",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 237,
          "start": 631.44,
          "end": 634.17,
          "en": "and we're now using React Router for sending",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 238,
          "start": 634.17,
          "end": 635.973,
          "en": "and for fetching data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 239,
          "start": 637.62,
          "end": 640.83,
          "en": "And as a result, you can see that our components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 240,
          "start": 640.83,
          "end": 642.66,
          "en": "got much leaner.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 241,
          "start": 642.66,
          "end": 644.64,
          "en": "We don't have to manually keep track",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 242,
          "start": 644.64,
          "end": 645.9,
          "en": "of what was entered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 243,
          "start": 645.9,
          "end": 648.36,
          "en": "We don't have to manually handle the form submission",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 244,
          "start": 648.36,
          "end": 650.28,
          "en": "and prevent the default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 245,
          "start": 650.28,
          "end": 651.84,
          "en": "We have to do none of that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 246,
          "start": 651.84,
          "end": 653.91,
          "en": "We instead embrace React Router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 247,
          "start": 653.91,
          "end": 655.74,
          "en": "for sending and getting data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 248,
          "start": 655.74,
          "end": 657.66,
          "en": "for navigation between pages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 249,
          "start": 657.66,
          "end": 660.3,
          "en": "and that's why React Router is awesome.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 250,
          "start": 660.3,
          "end": 663.06,
          "en": "Also, for simple demos like this one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 251,
          "start": 663.06,
          "end": 666.123,
          "en": "but especially, of course, for more complex websites.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
